From 3b81415fa6c87a7e5db3c194f830dbd41e573edc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:51:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/31] Nothing sent, no account: the private build, with what
 it may download

This build sends nothing to the original's services and asks for no
account: it is built without `online`, the original's private build,
which links none of that code: the A2 Tools account and sign-in, sharing
fights and the leaderboards (the "Help build the leaderboards?" prompt),
field boss and supply reports, party presence, the live boss connection,
the plugin catalog (this build's plugins come with its releases), the
supporter roster, Send Logs to Dev, Discord activity and the stream
overlay. The pages hide all of it (html.a2-offline).

A new feature `net` brings back the network client for what this build
downloads, and nothing else (net_guard.rs): its own releases (the update
check, the updater), the web services plugins list (a2.web.get, the
Market's prices), and the world boss and Abyss siege timers players
share (plain downloads of the feed files; nothing is reported back). The
client resolves only those hosts and follows redirects only to those
places, and each request checks its address. build_features tells the
pages `updates`, so the green button and Settings' update check stay. The
Arch package builds with `desktop,net`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
